        {
          "title": "SmolBSD – build your own minimal BSD system",
          "url": "https://smolbsd.org",
          "source": "Hacker News",
          "date": "2025-10-14T17:43:33Z",
          "language": "en",
          "section": "us_news",
          "raw_content": "smolBSD helps you create a minimal NetBSD-based virtual machine that boots and starts a service in a couple milliseconds. No prior NetBSD installation is required. Create and start a microvm from any GNU/Linux, NetBSD, or macOS system. PVH boot and various optimizations enable NetBSD/amd64 and NetBSD/i386 to directly boot QEMU or Firecracker in about 10 ms on modern x86 CPUs.",
